## What shipped

**Concept — "The ruled column."** The essay is about a form that produced restraint and a record that broke, so the page is built as a station logbook rather than as an article template.

- **Palette with a source:** rag paper, admiralty chart blue-grey ruling (a faint fixed rule runs behind the whole sheet), iron-gall ink, and one signal red used *only* for the light and the missing decade.
- **Type:** old-style serif at a 33.5rem measure, headline at ~4.75rem with the word "weather" in signal red; each section's opening line set in small caps instead of a drop cap; metadata in letterspaced grotesk small caps.
- **Byline as log column headers:** `WRITTEN BY / FILED / LENGTH` in ruled cells — the required byline, date, and read time, unchanged in content.
- **Marginal rail:** a left column carrying `Entry 01–04` stamps and a log datum per section. On phones it folds into an inline ruled stamp above each heading rather than stacking a dead column.
- **Peak — the record itself:** after "What automation actually removed," a ledger of one stroke per year, 1849→2026, that draws in on scroll. 1988–1997 is a visibly empty, red-washed column. The essay's thesis is the graphic.
- **Lede figure:** an engraved-plate SVG of the point, tower, and beam — ruled sky and broken chart-style sea lines. Caption preserved verbatim.
- Related articles set as a numbered index list (not a three-card row); subscribe input is a ruled underline; success state is a stamped "Entered in the book" entry.

**Preserved and verified in the render:** all four section headings and every paragraph unabridged, headline, standfirst, byline, lede image + caption, pull quote, all three footnotes, all three related items with descriptions and read times, the email form and its success state, and the four footer links.

**Verified in a real browser** at 1440, 390, and 320px: zero horizontal overflow at all three, no console or page errors, subscribe success state exercised at each width, and reduced-motion renders the ledger fully drawn (`matrix(1,0,0,1,0,0)`). Two bugs found by pixel inspection and fixed: sticky rail stamps were piling up over the Notes, and the mobile masthead was eating three rows — links now scroll on one line.

`npm run build` succeeds. Nothing committed.

**Direction note:** I built **Recommended**. Showcase would have added a scroll-authored sequence carrying the ledger strokes through the whole route as continuity; I did not pursue it because you couldn't confirm the direction in this session, and a reading route is better served by the restrained version. **Not pursued:** external photography for the lede — no licensed asset was available offline, so I built a deliberate engraved plate rather than a fake photograph; if you have a real image of the point, it drops straight into `LedePlate`.

